Subject: [PATCH 1/7] ci: cache cargo deps across runs and add cargo-audit
 workflow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each of the four CI jobs (lint, test 3-OS × 2-profile, replay, binaries)
previously recompiled every dependency from scratch on every push. Add
Swatinem/rust-cache@v2 after each 'Install the pinned toolchain' step,
keyed on Cargo.lock so a toolchain bump or lockfile change rotates the
cache cleanly.

Add a separate .github/workflows/audit.yml that runs 'cargo audit' on
every Cargo.lock change plus a nightly schedule. Read-only over the
lockfile: bumps nothing, changes no behavior, moves no goldens. The
project's dependency allow-list (plan §3.2) is strict, but transitive
vulnerabilities in serde/ron/wgpu/... would otherwise go undetected.

No source touched; no test impact.
---
 .github/workflows/audit.yml | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 .github/workflows/ci.yml    | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .github/workflows/audit.yml

diff --git a/.github/workflows/audit.yml b/.github/workflows/audit.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..29a644d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/audit.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+name: audit
+
+# Security audit of every crate in Cargo.lock. Read-only over the lockfile:
+# bumps nothing, changes no behavior, moves no goldens. The project's
+# dependency allow-list (plan §3.2) is strict — no rand/getrandom/ECS/game-
+# engine crates — but transitive vulnerabilities in serde/ron/wgpu/…
+# would otherwise go undetected. This job is the alarm, not the fix.
+
+on:
+  push:
+    paths:
+      - Cargo.lock
+      - .github/workflows/audit.yml
+  schedule:
+    # nightly at 06:00 UTC — catches advisories filed between pushes
+    - cron: "0 6 * * *"
+  workflow_dispatch:
+
+jobs:
+  audit:
+    name: cargo audit
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - name: Install cargo-audit
+        run: cargo install cargo-audit --locked
+      - name: Audit Cargo.lock for known vulnerabilities
+        run: cargo audit --deny warnings
