map_passability and map_buildability were ~20 lines each, 90% identical
— the only difference was '.passable' vs '.buildable' on the terrain
class lookup. Extract the shared body into map_flag(map, pick) and make
the two callers one-liner delegations.

Output bytes are unchanged: same loop order, same unwrap_or(false) for
unknown codes, same u8::from(bool). The content hash is computed by
encode_map in the same file, which reads map.grid directly (not via
these helpers), so the content hash is unaffected.

The 'content' crate IS scanned by tests/architecture_law.rs for banned
tokens (HashMap/HashSet/Instant/SystemTime/f32/f64). The refactor
introduces none. BTreeMap remains the only map type, as before.

No golden moves. fmt + clippy -D warnings + 352 dev tests green.
