Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(engine): replace no-op A15 checkpoint-trail assertion
 with a real one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A15 restart-cleanliness test (fresh_construction_with_the_same_seed_
produces_identical_hashes) had two pieces of dead code where a real
comparison was intended:

    // Same checkpoint trail.
    assert_eq!(oa.hashes.len(), oa.hashes.len());   // assert!(true)
    for (ha, _) in &oa.hashes {                       // empty body
        let _ = ha; // already asserted via state_hash above
    }

The assert_eq! compared a value's length to itself. The for loop had an
empty body and bound b's FrameOutcome was discarded ('let _ = b.advance').
The comment claimed 'Same checkpoint trail' was being checked, but it
wasn't.

Bind b's FrameOutcome, then assert the checkpoint trails are equal:

    let ob = b.advance(frame);
    ...
    assert_eq!(oa.hashes, ob.hashes, "the checkpoint trails must match");

Safe because the existing state_hash() assertion (a.state_hash() ==
b.state_hash()) already implies the checkpoints match — the checkpoint
value IS the state hash at checkpoint ticks. The new assertion just
makes the test's stated intent real and pins the trail comparison
explicitly. 48 engine tests still green (the A15 test included).

The 'engine' crate is NOT scanned by tests/architecture_law.rs (rendering
and timing legitimately use real clocks and float math there), so the
new assertion is unconstrained by the source bans. No golden moves.
