Four new property tests covering pub APIs whose contracts were only spot-
checked at one or two golden values:

1. hash_integer_writes_match_le_bytes — every integer write method
   (write_u8/u16/u32/u64/i32/i64) produces the same hash as writing the
   little-endian byte encoding of the same value. The unit test in
   hash.rs covers u32 and i64; this pins the remaining four. The state
   hash (sim/src/hash.rs) and the replay codec (replay/src/bytes.rs)
   both depend on this LE invariant.

2. abs_is_non_negative_and_idempotent — Fx::abs is non-negative for
   every input (saturating i32::MIN -> Fx::MAX per the documented
   contract), and idempotent: abs(abs(x)) == abs(x). Currently only
   tested at the extremes (extremes_never_panic) and one golden.

3. square_equals_mul_self — Fx::square delegates to mul(self); this
   pins the delegation so a future 'optimized' square path cannot
   silently diverge from mul.

4. vec_dist_matches_subtraction_then_length — Vec2Fx::dist(a, b) ==
   (a - b).len() for arbitrary inputs in the non-saturating range. The
   docstring on dist claims this equivalence; the only unit test
   (three_four_five_is_exact) covers a == ZERO. This pins it for
   arbitrary a, b.

Tests-only. No production code touched. No golden moves. 19 fx
property tests green (was 15).
